# General
As a finance team member, I want uploaded invoices to be automatically archived in Google Drive so that financial documentation is stored redundantly and can still be recovered if the local application storage is lost.

Each uploaded invoice is first stored locally by PayTrack. If Google Drive archiving is enabled, the already saved local invoice is then uploaded to the configured Google Drive folder of the racing team.

Target storage architecture:

`<year>/<month>/<invoice-file-name>`

Example:

`2026/March/invoice_INV-123_20260527_194127.pdf`

The Google Drive integration uses a service account only. OAuth is not supported anymore because this is a backend-to-Drive archiving feature and should not depend on a user login flow.

Configuration is available through `appsettings.json`, `appsettings.Development.json`, and `.env` overrides:

- `GoogleDrive:Enabled`
- `GoogleDrive:RootFolderId`
- `GoogleDrive:ServiceAccountKeyPath`
- `GoogleDrive:ServiceAccountKeyBase64`

`ServiceAccountKeyPath` and `ServiceAccountKeyBase64` are mutually exclusive. The application throws a configuration error if both are set at the same time.

For local testing, the service account JSON can be stored as a base64 value in development settings. For real deployment, the TUW/racing team credentials can be provided through normal configuration or environment variables.

Failure policy:

If the Google Drive upload fails, the invoice upload must still succeed from the user perspective. The file remains stored locally, the Drive failure is logged, and PayTrack sends an email notification to `gitlab@racing.tuwien.ac.at` with the invoice attached so an admin can manually upload it later. The invoice has the following structure:
![image](/uploads/6b1924a9efc7cad062afb9ccb4f3de3a/image.png){width=900 height=187}

Implementation details:

- Google Drive SDK dependency was added.
- Google Drive upload logic was extracted into `IGoogleDriveArchiveClient` / `GoogleDriveArchiveClient`.
- `FileRepository.SaveFile(...)` now only coordinates local saving and optional archiving.
- Google Drive folders are created or reused automatically by year and month.
- Upload uses the locally saved file path, so no request stream reset is needed anymore.
- Google Drive query values are escaped before folder lookup.
- Email notification supports file attachments.
- Archive failures do not block invoice submission.
- Tests mock the Google Drive archive client and verify local save, archive calls, and failure notification behavior.

