# Google Drive Upload Setup Guide

This feature is disabled by default. To make automatic Drive archiving work locally, each developer needs their own `.env` configuration because secrets and Drive folder IDs are not committed.

### Required Google Drive Folder

1. Open Google Drive with the account that should own the uploaded archive files.
2. Create one root archive folder, for example: `PayTrack Archive`
3. Open the folder and copy its folder ID from the URL. Example:
`https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1abcDEFghiJKLmnoPQRstuVWxyz`. The folder ID then is: `1abcDEFghiJKLmnoPQRstuVWxyz`. The backend will automatically create subfolders inside this root folder: `PayTrack Archive/2026/May/uploaded-invoice.pdf`.

### Required .env Section
Add the following values to your local .env file:
```
GOOGLE_DRIVE_ENABLED=true
GOOGLE_DRIVE_AUTHENTICATION_MODE=OAuth
GOOGLE_DRIVE_ROOT_FOLDER_ID=your_drive_folder_id_here
GOOGLE_DRIVE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRETS_PATH=path/to/oauth-client-secrets.json
GOOGLE_DRIVE_OAUTH_TOKEN_STORE_PATH=google-drive-token
```

### OAuth Client Secrets
Each developer needs a Google OAuth client secrets JSON file.
The file path must match:
```
GOOGLE_DRIVE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRETS_PATH=path/to/oauth-client-secrets.json
```
Do not commit this JSON file!

### Verify The Setup
1. Start the backend.
2. Upload an invoice/receipt through the normal payment request flow.
3. On the first OAuth run, approve access with the Google account that owns the archive folder.
4. Check the configured Drive folder.
5. Confirm that the file appears under the generated year/month folder.

### Disable Drive Upload Again
Set:
```
GOOGLE_DRIVE_ENABLED=false
```
Expected behavior: files are still stored locally, but no Google Drive upload is attempted.

